The record
Stack the member totals into a vector \(u_c = (Y_c, n_c, n_c T_c, N_c, D_c)\) with \(K = 5\) components. A cell \(k = (z, h)\) is an arm \(z\) crossed with a stratum \(h\), for example a cohort. For each cell we store the count \(G_k\), the sum \(\sum_{c \in k} u_c\) and the sum of outer products \(\sum_{c \in k} u_c u_c^\top\). That is \(1 + K + K(K+1)/2 = 21\) numbers per cell, regardless of the number of members.
The compression is another single pass, this time over members, so it is also a short loop.


Code
#include &lt;Rcpp.h&gt;
using namespace Rcpp;

// Clusters to the compressed record in one pass: per cell, the count G_k, the sums of u,
// and the sums of u_a u_b for a &lt;= b, the upper triangle of the sum of u u^T.
// [[Rcpp::export]]
NumericMatrix compress_cells(IntegerVector cell, NumericMatrix U, int n_cells) {
  int n = U.nrow(), K = U.ncol();
  NumericMatrix out(n_cells, 1 + K + K * (K + 1) / 2);
  for (int i = 0; i &lt; n; i++) {
    int g = cell[i] - 1, col = 1 + K;
    out(g, 0) += 1;
    for (int a = 0; a &lt; K; a++) {
      out(g, 1 + a) += U(i, a);
      for (int b = a; b &lt; K; b++) out(g, col++) += U(i, a) * U(i, b);
    }
  }
  return out;
}




Code
compress &lt;- function(clusters, keys, u_cols) {
  groups &lt;- group_by(clusters, across(all_of(keys)))
  record &lt;- compress_cells(group_indices(groups), as.matrix(clusters[u_cols]), n_groups(groups))
  K &lt;- length(u_cols)
  pairs &lt;- unlist(map(1:K, \(a) paste0(u_cols[a], "_", u_cols[a:K])))
  colnames(record) &lt;- c("G", paste0("S1_", u_cols), paste0("S2_", pairs))
  bind_cols(group_keys(groups), as_tibble(record))
}

